      intro: "Classical fiqh — particularly the well-documented Ḥanbalī treatment in Ibn Qudāmah's Al-Mughnī — sets out specific, mandatory conditions before this relationship becomes lawful at all. Failing any one of them collapses the act into zinā, with real legal consequences attached, as ash-Shāfiʿī's own rulings on rape make explicit.",
